// src/user/compositor/xdg_shell_states.pdx -- Wave0-B6-07 (paideia-os #2260)
//
// KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE = 0x1C4, derived over KIND_WINDOW (paideia-os
// #2254 = G7-M3-001 / B6-05, landed in this same Wave-0 batch).
//
// Design authority:
//   * design/compositor/pwp-spec-vocabulary.md §2.7 KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE
//     and KIND_XDG_POPUP -- the XDG-shell-equivalent surface pair. This
//     landing implements the TOPLEVEL_STATE half; KIND_XDG_POPUP is a
//     sibling landing (G7-M4-002, #2261).
//
// PURPOSE. A derived-kind capability that names one toplevel window's
// state-machine position (normal / maximized / fullscreen / minimized /
// tiled-{left,right,top,bottom}), its current window geometry expressed
// EXCLUDING client-side decoration, its currently-bound interactive
// resize edges, and its associated output. Held per-window by the
// toolkit; the compositor consumes it to decide layer promotion,
// direct-scanout candidacy, and hardware-plane assignment.
//
// SEPARATION FROM KIND_WINDOW (spec §2.7). Toplevel-state is a SEPARATE
// derived kind, not a set of fields on KIND_WINDOW, so that a tiling-
// only toolkit (or a headless render harness) can hold KIND_WINDOW
// without ever minting a toplevel-state cap. That factoring also lets
// the same window carry two independent state observers (e.g. a session
// manager and a compositor) without contending on window-cap ownership.
//
// NOVEL-CLEAN CHOICES.
//   * GEOMETRY EXCLUDES CSD. There is no server-side decoration in this
//     window system; the client owns every pixel inside its geometry
//     rect (this is the WAYLAND design closest to reality, and the one
//     GNOME/GTK, Firefox, and Chromium have converged on). Excluding
//     CSD from the wire geometry means the shell never confuses "window
//     size with titlebar" vs "window size without titlebar" -- a bug
//     class every X11 shell has re-hit.
//   * TILING STATES FIRST-CLASS. TILED_{LEFT,RIGHT,TOP,BOTTOM} are
//     enumerated state values, not a compositor extension. A tiling
//     manager sets state to TILED_LEFT and geometry to the left-half
//     rect; there is no separate "tiling protocol" the compositor and
//     client have to negotiate (a common Wayland pitfall -- xdg-tiling
//     never standardised, so every compositor invented its own).
//
// =============================================================================
// SLOT ALLOCATION -- KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE = 0x1C4
// =============================================================================
//
// 0x1C4 is verified free at landing time by grep across src/ and
// design/architecture/. It sits in the G7+ compositor band that opens
// after the R101/R103/R104/R105 GUI kernel block (0x1AE..0x1B1), the
// R90-XREPO.LV11 block (0x1B2..0x1B4), and the G6 colour block
// (0x1B5..0x1B7). The Wave-0 Batch-6 dispatcher allocates 0x1C0..0x1CF
// to the compositor vocabulary landings (KIND_SURFACE, KIND_WINDOW,
// KIND_LAYER_TREE, ...); this row occupies slot 0x1C4 per the batch's
// row assignments. Main should reconcile the "Next free derived-kind
// tag" line in design/architecture/next-wave-derived-kinds.md at the
// end of this batch by advancing it past the Batch-6 block.
//
// =============================================================================
// DERIVATION OVER KIND_WINDOW
// =============================================================================
//
// Parent kind is KIND_WINDOW (the G7-M3-001 landing; spec §2.4 makes
// WINDOW the toplevel-window authority and pins it as the parent of the
// TOPLEVEL_STATE / POPUP pair in §2.7). Mint requires the parent-window
// cap to carry RIGHT_MINT: only the process that authored the window
// (or a delegate holding a re-mint-carrying window cap) may create a
// state edge for it. This mirrors the parent-carries-MINT gate every
// derived-kind in this tree uses (kind_gpu_bo over KIND_MEMORY,
// kind_tui_canvas over KIND_MEMORY, kind_reference_display over
// KIND_MEMORY). The kernel-side dispatch handler + parent-kind check
// lands as a follow-up milestone; this file is the SCHEMA SEED that
// registers the ordinal, publishes the row layout and rights bits, and
// exposes the pure schema helpers (factory, tiled predicate, effective-
// geometry accessor) every downstream landing will read from.
//
// =============================================================================
// ROW LAYOUT -- 64 BYTES (one cache line)
// =============================================================================
//
//   [+0]  header:        in_use[63:56] | reserved[55:0]
//   [+8]  state_id:      u64, kernel-assigned monotonic, never 0
//   [+16] parent_pack:   window_kind_id[31:0] | output_kind_id[63:32]
//                        (output_kind_id == 0 means "auto" -- compositor
//                        picks the output at state-apply time)
//   [+24] state_pack:    state[7:0] | active_resize_edges[15:8] |
//                        reserved[63:16]
//   [+32] geom_xy:       geometry_x[31:0] (i32) | geometry_y[63:32] (i32)
//   [+40] geom_wh:       geometry_w[31:0] (i32) | geometry_h[63:32] (i32)
//   [+48] transitions:   u64, running state-change count (bumped by the
//                        substrate on every xdg_toplevel_state_set)
//   [+56] reserved:      u64 (future: parent-window state_id for modality
//                        anchoring, per spec §2.4's parent-window edge)
//
// GEOMETRY IS SIGNED (i32 per coord). Negative coordinates are permitted
// so a window can straddle output boundaries in a multi-output layout
// (Wayland's xdg_surface.set_window_geometry uses signed coords for the
// same reason). Width/height must be non-negative (a zero-sized
// geometry is legal ONLY for MINIMIZED); the validator enforces that
// separately.
//
// GEOMETRY EXCLUDES CSD. The header's guarantee: the (x, y, w, h)
// stored here is the window's pixel space EXCLUDING any client-side
// decoration the toolkit may draw. A toolkit that paints a shadow
// outside its geometry (a common effect) computes the shadow rect
// independently; the compositor's hit-testing, focus targeting, and
// hardware-plane candidacy all use the geometry stored here.
//
// EFFECTIVE-GEOMETRY SEMANTICS. The compositor is responsible for
// updating the stored geometry to match the state's constraint at
// every state transition: for MAXIMIZED the stored rect IS the
// output's full usable area (minus reserved regions); for TILED_LEFT
// the stored rect IS the left half of the target output; for
// MINIMIZED the stored rect is (0, 0, 0, 0). The
// xdg_toplevel_state_effective_geometry accessor returns the stored
// rect as-is for every non-MINIMIZED state (the compositor already
// placed it), and returns (0, 0, 0, 0) for MINIMIZED. This factoring
// keeps schema helpers pure (no output-table lookup at query time) and
// puts the tiling arithmetic where it belongs: in the compositor's
// layout policy.

module XdgShellStates = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1 -- KIND ORDINAL + PARENT + POOL CEILING
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE      : u64 = 0x1C4
  pub let KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE_BASE : u64 = 0x1C1   // = KIND_WINDOW slot in the G7 batch (B6-05, #2254)

  // Pool ceiling. 32 concurrent toplevel-state rows -- a typical
  // desktop with 8..12 open windows fits comfortably, and 32 is the
  // per-user seat's realistic ceiling before workspace switching should
  // page state out. 32 * 64 = 2048 bytes -- one 2 KiB slab.
  pub let XSS_MAX       : u64 = 32
  pub let XSS_ROW_BYTES : u64 = 64

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- RIGHTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Four rights, each addressable independently:
  //   RIGHT_SET_STATE                -- change the enum value
  //   RIGHT_SET_GEOMETRY_EXCL        -- change the (x, y, w, h) rect
  //                                     (EXCL suffix pins the CSD-excluded
  //                                     coordinate space)
  //   RIGHT_QUERY_STATE              -- read state + geometry + edges
  //   RIGHT_REQUEST_INTERACTIVE_RESIZE -- send a start-resize request
  //                                     naming an edge bitmask
  //
  // Kernel-standard rights (R_XSS_MINT, R_XSS_REVOKE, R_XSS_OBSERVE)
  // occupy the usual conventional bits so a substrate that already
  // knows those slots can dispatch without a rights-table remap.

  pub let RIGHT_SET_STATE                  : u64 = 0x001
  pub let RIGHT_SET_GEOMETRY_EXCL          : u64 = 0x002
  pub let RIGHT_QUERY_STATE                : u64 = 0x004
  pub let RIGHT_REQUEST_INTERACTIVE_RESIZE : u64 = 0x008
  pub let R_XSS_MINT                       : u64 = 0x200
  pub let R_XSS_REVOKE                     : u64 = 0x010
  pub let R_XSS_OBSERVE                    : u64 = 0x400
  pub let R_XSS_ALL                        : u64 = 0x61F  // 0x001|0x002|0x004|0x008|0x010|0x200|0x400

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- TOPLEVEL STATE ENUM
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Ordinal values are stable and MUST NOT be renumbered -- they ride
  // the wire in the state[7:0] field of the row's [+24] word. The
  // enumeration is exhaustive at this landing; a future revision that
  // adds e.g. TILED_QUARTER_TL would extend past 7, and every consumer
  // of xdg_toplevel_state_is_tiled would need to widen its predicate.

  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_NORMAL       : u64 = 0
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_MAXIMIZED    : u64 = 1
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_FULLSCREEN   : u64 = 2
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_MINIMIZED    : u64 = 3
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_LEFT   : u64 = 4
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_RIGHT  : u64 = 5
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_TOP    : u64 = 6
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_BOTTOM : u64 = 7
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_MAX          : u64 = 7

  // Convenience predicate: first tiled state is 4.
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_FIRST  : u64 = 4
  pub let TOPLEVEL_STATE_TILED_LAST   : u64 = 7

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 4 -- INTERACTIVE-RESIZE EDGE BITMASK
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Bit 0 = TOP, bit 1 = BOTTOM, bit 2 = LEFT, bit 3 = RIGHT. Corners
  // are OR of two edges (e.g. top-left = 0x05 = TOP | LEFT). The full
  // set 0x0F is the "resize from any edge" hint. Bit 4..7 reserved for
  // future edge kinds (e.g. rotation handles); the validator refuses
  // any bit outside 0x0F.

  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_NONE        : u64 = 0x00
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_TOP         : u64 = 0x01
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_BOTTOM      : u64 = 0x02
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_LEFT        : u64 = 0x04
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_RIGHT       : u64 = 0x08
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_TOP_LEFT    : u64 = 0x05  // TOP | LEFT
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_TOP_RIGHT   : u64 = 0x09  // TOP | RIGHT
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_BOTTOM_LEFT : u64 = 0x06  // BOTTOM | LEFT
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_BOTTOM_RIGHT: u64 = 0x0A  // BOTTOM | RIGHT
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_ALL         : u64 = 0x0F  // TOP|BOTTOM|LEFT|RIGHT
  pub let RESIZE_EDGE_MASK        : u64 = 0x0F  // valid-bits mask

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 5 -- ROW LAYOUT OFFSETS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // These offsets are the machine-readable spelling of the row layout
  // documented in the file header. Every producer / consumer of a row
  // reads through THESE constants, not through hand-rolled +8 arithmetic.

  pub let XSS_OFF_HEADER      : u64 = 0
  pub let XSS_OFF_STATE_ID    : u64 = 8
  pub let XSS_OFF_PARENT_PACK : u64 = 16
  pub let XSS_OFF_STATE_PACK  : u64 = 24
  pub let XSS_OFF_GEOM_XY     : u64 = 32
  pub let XSS_OFF_GEOM_WH     : u64 = 40
  pub let XSS_OFF_TRANSITIONS : u64 = 48
  pub let XSS_OFF_RESERVED    : u64 = 56

  // Sub-word offsets inside the packed words. `state` occupies byte 0
  // of the state_pack word; `active_resize_edges` occupies byte 1.
  // These constants let a consumer that only wants one byte skip the
  // full u64 unpack and issue a targeted byte-load instead.
  pub let XSS_STATE_PACK_STATE_BYTE : u64 = 24   // = XSS_OFF_STATE_PACK + 0
  pub let XSS_STATE_PACK_EDGES_BYTE : u64 = 25   // = XSS_OFF_STATE_PACK + 1

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 6 -- OP TAGS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Kernel dispatch surface. Every op is arity-one from the caller's
  // perspective; op_arg semantics vary by op and are documented at each
  // op tag. Dispatch lands in a follow-up milestone.

  pub let XSS_OP_SET_STATE          : u64 = 0   // op_arg = new state ordinal
  pub let XSS_OP_SET_GEOMETRY       : u64 = 1   // op_arg = geometry buffer ptr (4 i32s)
  pub let XSS_OP_SET_EDGES          : u64 = 2   // op_arg = edge bitmask
  pub let XSS_OP_SET_OUTPUT         : u64 = 3   // op_arg = output kind_id (0 = auto)
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_STATE        : u64 = 4   // -> state ordinal
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_GEOMETRY     : u64 = 5   // op_arg = out ptr (4 i32s)
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_EDGES        : u64 = 6   // -> edge bitmask
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_OUTPUT       : u64 = 7   // -> output kind_id
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_STATE_ID     : u64 = 8   // -> row's state_id
  pub let XSS_OP_QUERY_WINDOW_ID    : u64 = 9   // -> parent window kind_id
  pub let XSS_OP_REQUEST_INTERACTIVE_RESIZE : u64 = 10  // op_arg = edge bitmask
  pub let XSS_OP_DEBUG_PRINT        : u64 = 11  // R_XSS_OBSERVE; row dump
  pub let XSS_OP_MAX                : u64 = 11

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 7 -- FAILURE TAXONOMY -- 0xFFFFEA40..0xFFFFEA4F
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // A fresh 16-wide band verified free at landing time by grep across
  // src/kernel/core/cap/*.pdx + src/user/**/*.pdx + tests/**/*.pdx.
  // 0xFFFFEA50..0xFFFFEA5F is KIND_REFERENCE_DISPLAY (G6-M6-001);
  // 0xFFFFEA40..0xFFFFEA4F is the next page below and is unclaimed.

  pub let XSS_OK                    : u64 = 0
  pub let XSS_TAIL_ENOSPC           : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4F
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_WINDOW       : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4E
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_RIGHTS       : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4D
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_STATE        : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4C
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_GEOMETRY     : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4B
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_EDGES        : u64 = 0xFFFFEA4A
  pub let XSS_MINT_BAD_OUTPUT       : u64 = 0xFFFFEA49
  pub let XSS_BAD_SLOT              : u64 = 0xFFFFEA48
  pub let XSS_BAD_RIGHTS            : u64 = 0xFFFFEA47
  pub let XSS_WRONG_KIND            : u64 = 0xFFFFEA46
  pub let XSS_REVOKE_ALREADY        : u64 = 0xFFFFEA45
  pub let XSS_UNSUP_OP              : u64 = 0xFFFFEA44
  pub let XSS_BAD_ARG               : u64 = 0xFFFFEA43
  pub let XSS_DECODE_BAD            : u64 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 8 -- STATS COUNTER SLOTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The kernel-side substrate will publish a _xss_stats [u64; 8] table
  // in a follow-up milestone; the slot indices are named here so cross-
  // module bumpers agree.

  pub let XSS_ST_MINTS        : u64 = 0
  pub let XSS_ST_REVOKES      : u64 = 1
  pub let XSS_ST_TRANSITIONS  : u64 = 2   // successful xdg_toplevel_state_set calls
  pub let XSS_ST_GEOM_SETS    : u64 = 3   // successful geometry updates
  pub let XSS_ST_RESIZE_REQS  : u64 = 4   // interactive-resize requests granted
  pub let XSS_ST_REFUSED      : u64 = 5
  pub let XSS_ST_MAX          : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 9 -- FINGERPRINT (one line, legacy-suffixed)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Emitted once on successful mint by the future substrate. The
  // legacy-suffix convention is what tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh
  // enumerates, so this literal is the machine-checkable name of the
  // milestone. No fingerprint on the set / query / revoke paths.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_mint_ok_msg : [u8; 59] = "xdg toplevel state mint ok [legacy: XDG TOP STATE MINT OK]\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 10 -- VALIDATORS (pure leaves, small immediates)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every function in this section is a pure unsafe-bodied leaf with
  // small immediates, returns in rax, and clobbers only rax + one
  // scratch. No `test`, no `add reg, [mem]` -- per issue's coding
  // budget. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_ per row's reserved-label
  // discipline.

  // xdg_shell_states_state_valid(s) -> 1 iff s in [0, TOPLEVEL_STATE_MAX].
  pub let xdg_shell_states_state_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (s: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): state ordinal validator. Admits 0..7 (NORMAL through TILED_BOTTOM). Small immediates so no MOVABS. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_sv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 7;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_sv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_states_sv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_edges_valid(e) -> 1 iff e & ~RESIZE_EDGE_MASK == 0.
  // Uses cmp against 0 rather than `test` per issue's coding budget.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_edges_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (e: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): resize-edge bitmask validator. Admits any subset of RESIZE_EDGE_MASK (0x0F); every bit outside 0x0F is refused. Uses `mov r10, ~mask` folded into small immediate 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0 via NOT of a small imm to sidestep MOVABS. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_ev_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, rdi;
        mov r10, 0x0F;
        not r10;                    // r10 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0
        and rax, r10;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne xdg_shell_states_ev_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_states_ev_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_geom_wh_valid(w, h) -> 1 iff w >= 0 && h >= 0 AND
  // each fits in i32 (i.e. within [0, 0x7FFFFFFF]). Zero w or h is
  // legal (a MINIMIZED window has a zero-sized geometry rect); the
  // per-state cross-check that MINIMIZED implies (0,0,0,0) lives at
  // the mint gate, not here.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_geom_wh_valid : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (w: u64) (h: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): geometry width/height validator. Admits w,h in [0, 0x7FFFFFFF] (fits signed i32, non-negative). Uses ja against 0x7FFFFFFF (32-bit imm -> mov r64, imm32 sign-extends but 0x7FFFFFFF is positive so preserved). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_gv_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0x7FFFFFFF;
        cmp rdi, r10;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_gv_no;
        cmp rsi, r10;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_gv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_states_gv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 11 -- PACKERS
  // ==========================================================================

  // xdg_shell_states_parent_pack(window_kind_id, output_kind_id) ->
  // window_kind_id[31:0] | output_kind_id[63:32]. Both fields masked
  // to 32 bits before the shift so an out-of-range argument cannot
  // smear into a neighbour.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_parent_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (window_kind_id: u64) (output_kind_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): pack window_kind_id[31:0] | output_kind_id[63:32] per row layout at [+16]. Both fields masked to 32 bits with 0xFFFFFFFF (mov r64, imm32 sign-extends 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF but the mask is applied via AND which truncates correctly). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_pp_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;         // mask via mov r10, imm32 sign-extends to all-ones; correct as an AND mask
        mov rax, rsi;                // output_kind_id
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                // window_kind_id
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_state_pack(state, edges) -> state[7:0] |
  // active_resize_edges[15:8] | reserved[63:16]. Both fields masked
  // to 8 bits.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_state_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (state: u64) (edges: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): pack state[7:0] | edges[15:8] per row layout at [+24]. Reserved [63:16] left zero. Both fields masked to 8 bits so an out-of-range argument cannot smear. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_stp_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, rsi;                // edges
        and rax, 0xFF;
        shl rax, 8;
        mov r10, rdi;                // state
        and r10, 0xFF;
        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_geom_xy_pack(gx, gy) -> gx[31:0] | gy[63:32].
  // Coordinates are i32; the low 32 bits of each argument are taken
  // verbatim, sign bit included, so a negative coord round-trips
  // correctly through the pack/unpack pair.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_geom_xy_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (gx: u64) (gy: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): pack gx[31:0] | gy[63:32] per row layout at [+32]. Signed i32 coords: low 32 bits taken verbatim so a negative value round-trips (interpreted as u32 in the wire word, re-interpreted as i32 by the reader). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_gxy_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        mov rax, rsi;                // gy
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                // gx
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_geom_wh_pack(gw, gh) -> gw[31:0] | gh[63:32].
  // Mirror of _geom_xy_pack; separate name to keep call sites self-
  // documenting.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_geom_wh_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (gw: u64) (gh: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): pack gw[31:0] | gh[63:32] per row layout at [+40]. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_gwh_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        mov rax, rsi;                // gh
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                // gw
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_states_hdr_pack() -> canonical row header (in_use bit
  // set by the mint gate's tail_alloc, not here). Mirror of
  // kind_tui_canvas's tui_hdr_pack: returns 0 today.
  pub let xdg_shell_states_hdr_pack : () -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): canonical row header. Only in_use is ever written (by tail_alloc), low 56 bits stay 0. Mirrors kind_tui_canvas.pdx tui_hdr_pack. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_hp_.",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 12 -- FACTORY: xdg_toplevel_state_set(row_ptr, state, geom_ptr)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Writes state + geometry (from a caller-provided 16-byte buffer
  // holding x, y, w, h as four i32s) into an already-allocated row.
  // Does NOT allocate a row (that is the mint gate's job) and does
  // NOT bump the transitions counter (the substrate's dispatch handler
  // owns counter updates). Validates state ordinal + width/height;
  // refuses the write on failure and leaves the row untouched.
  //
  // Signature: (row_ptr: u64, state: u64, geom_ptr: u64) -> u64
  //   * row_ptr:  pointer to a 64-byte row already tail-allocated
  //   * state:    the new ToplevelState ordinal
  //   * geom_ptr: pointer to 4 packed i32s -- [x, y, w, h]
  //   * returns:  XSS_OK on success; XSS_BAD_ARG on invalid state
  //               or w/h; row is untouched on failure.
  pub let xdg_toplevel_state_set : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) (state: u64) (geom_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): factory that writes state + geometry into an existing row. Validates state in [0,7] and w/h in [0, i32 max] before any store. Uses `cmp reg, imm`+`ja` (never `test`). Loads x,y,w,h from geom_ptr as four dword-shaped fetches then reassembles into the two packed u64s at row_ptr+32 and row_ptr+40; the assembly uses `mov e/r*d, [mem]` semantics implied by the 32-bit dest (proven pattern via cap_net_privileged.pdx's `mov eax, [rdi + 0]`) rather than `add reg, [mem]`. Scratch registers: rax, r8, r9, r10, r11 (all SysV caller-saved). NO clobber of rbx/rbp/r12-r15 (SysV callee-saved). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_ts_.",
      block: {
        // Validate state in [0, 7].
        cmp rsi, 7;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_ts_bad;

        // Validate w (i32 at geom_ptr + 8) in [0, 0x7FFFFFFF].
        mov r10d, [rdx + 8];
        mov r11, 0x7FFFFFFF;
        cmp r10, r11;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_ts_bad;

        // Validate h (i32 at geom_ptr + 12) in [0, 0x7FFFFFFF].
        mov r10d, [rdx + 12];
        cmp r10, r11;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_ts_bad;

        // ---- All validated. Commit the writes. ----

        // state_pack write: state[7:0] | edges_preserved[15:8] | reserved.
        // We read the existing state_pack (to preserve the edges byte
        // and any future reserved bits), clear byte 0, then OR the new
        // state ordinal in.
        mov r10, [rdi + 24];
        // Mask off low byte: r10 &= ~0xFF via mov + not on a small imm.
        mov r11, 0xFF;
        not r11;                        // r11 = ~0xFF = 0xFFFF...FF00
        and r10, r11;
        mov r8, rsi;                    // new state (r8 is SysV caller-saved)
        and r8, 0xFF;
        or  r10, r8;
        mov [rdi + 24], r10;

        // geom_xy_pack write from geom_ptr[0..8] -> row_ptr[+32].
        // Load 32-bit x into r10 (zero-extends), 32-bit y into r11.
        mov r10d, [rdx + 0];            // x (i32; zero-extended to r10 as u32)
        mov r11d, [rdx + 4];            // y
        shl r11, 32;
        or  r10, r11;
        mov [rdi + 32], r10;

        // geom_wh_pack write from geom_ptr[8..16] -> row_ptr[+40].
        mov r10d, [rdx + 8];            // w
        mov r11d, [rdx + 12];           // h
        shl r11, 32;
        or  r10, r11;
        mov [rdi + 40], r10;

        xor rax, rax;                   // XSS_OK = 0
        ret;

      xdg_shell_states_ts_bad:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEA43;            // XSS_BAD_ARG
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 13 -- QUERY: xdg_toplevel_state_is_tiled(row_ptr) -> bool
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Returns 1 if the row's state is any of TILED_LEFT / TILED_RIGHT /
  // TILED_TOP / TILED_BOTTOM (ordinals 4..7). Returns 0 otherwise.
  // Reads one byte from the row's state_pack word -- no full u64
  // unpack needed.
  pub let xdg_toplevel_state_is_tiled : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): predicate returning 1 iff state in {TILED_LEFT..TILED_BOTTOM} (ordinals 4..7). Reads the full state_pack u64 at row_ptr + 24 then masks to the low byte with AND 0xFF (encoder-conservative: same posture kind_tui_canvas.pdx uses for sub-byte state extraction, avoids a `movzx r64, byte ptr [mem]` spelling that is not established in this tree). Uses `cmp reg, imm`+`jb`+`ja` -- no `test`. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_it_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 24];
        and rax, 0xFF;
        cmp rax, 4;
        jb  xdg_shell_states_it_no;
        cmp rax, 7;
        ja  xdg_shell_states_it_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_states_it_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 14 -- QUERY: xdg_toplevel_state_effective_geometry
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Writes the effective (x, y, w, h) into a caller-provided 16-byte
  // buffer (out_ptr, four i32s). Semantics:
  //   * MINIMIZED: writes (0, 0, 0, 0) -- window is hidden.
  //   * all other states: writes the stored geometry as-is (the
  //     compositor is responsible for updating stored geometry at
  //     each state transition to match the state's constraint;
  //     see header comment §"EFFECTIVE-GEOMETRY SEMANTICS").
  //
  // Signature: (row_ptr, out_ptr) -> u64
  //   * returns XSS_OK on success.
  pub let xdg_toplevel_state_effective_geometry : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) (out_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-001 (#2260): effective-geometry accessor. Reads the state_pack u64 at row_ptr + 24, masks to low byte with AND 0xFF (same pattern as xdg_toplevel_state_is_tiled above); if state == 3 (MINIMIZED) writes zeros to out_ptr[0..16], otherwise copies row_ptr[+32..+48] to out_ptr[0..16] via two u64 loads + two u64 stores. Uses `mov r64, [mem]` and `mov [mem], r64` -- no `add reg, [mem]`, no `test`. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_states_eg_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 24];               // state_pack
        and rax, 0xFF;                     // state byte
        cmp rax, 3;                        // MINIMIZED
        je  xdg_shell_states_eg_minimized;

        // Non-minimized: mirror stored geometry to out_ptr.
        mov r10, [rdi + 32];               // geom_xy
        mov [rsi + 0], r10;
        mov r10, [rdi + 40];               // geom_wh
        mov [rsi + 8], r10;
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;

      xdg_shell_states_eg_minimized:
        // Write four zero i32s.
        xor r10, r10;
        mov [rsi + 0], r10;
        mov [rsi + 8], r10;
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }
}
